Monolayer BN - BGW/Sigma
========================

In this directory we calculate the GW quasiparticle energies for BN using the
Sigma code from BerkeleyGW.


Instructions
------------

  1. Notice which files need to be linked.

  2. Take a look at ``sigma.inp``. You can calculate Sigma for any k-points in
     ``WFN_inner``. Use the tool ``wfn_rho_vxc_info.x`` to see which points are
     present in ``WFN_inner``, and make sure all k-points in ``sigma.inp`` are present
     in ``WFN_co``.

  3. Run the sigma calculation using ``./01-run_sigma.qsub``. This will
     take less than a minute.

  4. Take a look at your output file ``sigma.out``. Are there any warnings?

  5. We will now plot the GW-corrected band structure for BN. Go to the folder
     ``bandstructure/`` and follow the instructions.
